1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,900
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:41,400
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,533 --> 00:00:42,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:44,933 --> 00:00:46,200
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,233 --> 00:00:57,367
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,267
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,500
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,633 --> 00:01:01,967
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:06,900
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,933 --> 00:01:11,833
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:12,767 --> 00:01:16,967
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:19,867
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,333
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,467 --> 00:01:24,867
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,100
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,033 --> 00:01:32,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:33,067 --> 00:01:34,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:36,133
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,267 --> 00:01:37,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,533 --> 00:01:38,633
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:40,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,067 --> 00:01:48,100
<i>I caught him.
But a bunch of people came.</i>

24
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:50,633
<i>They shot at me.
That's why they got him!</i>

25
00:01:50,767 --> 00:01:52,500
<i> We went up against big people.</i>

26
00:01:52,633 --> 00:01:54,100
<i>And they look like
an organized syndicate.</i>

27
00:01:54,233 --> 00:01:58,400
<i>If that lawyer screws up,
I know another way.</i>

28
00:01:58,533 --> 00:02:00,633
<i> The woman who caught Victor</i>

29
00:02:00,767 --> 00:02:03,233
<i>is General Ricardo Jacinto's
daughter.</i>

30
00:02:03,367 --> 00:02:05,167
<i>You sure you know
who you're messing with?</i>

31
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:06,833
<i>Are you sure about
your investigation?</i>

32
00:02:06,967 --> 00:02:09,500
<i>We did our homework.
Our op was completely legit.</i>

33
00:02:09,633 --> 00:02:11,567
<i>Are we still doing
everything wrong?</i>

34
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:14,567
<i>Dad sees things
we don't, Sam.</i>

35
00:02:14,733 --> 00:02:17,133
<i>We're still new to the force.
He's the former chief.</i>

36
00:02:17,267 --> 00:02:20,167
<i>My team and I caught
a major criminal.</i>

37
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:25,667
<i>You forgot your stubbornness
destroyed this family!</i>

38
00:02:31,867 --> 00:02:33,933
[LIQUID POURING]

39
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:37,000
[DOOR CLOSES]

40
00:02:37,133 --> 00:02:40,133
Have you talked to Ricardo yet?

41
00:02:40,267 --> 00:02:41,300
[EXHALES SOFTLY]

42
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:43,467
He said he'd see
what he can do.

43
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,933
And if that doesn't work?

44
00:02:45,067 --> 00:02:46,867
He can't say no to me.

45
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,800
He might've played me before,
but not anymore.

46
00:02:51,733 --> 00:02:56,233
I have more money now,
and way more power.

47
00:02:56,367 --> 00:03:00,367
And it's all because of you
and our businesses.

48
00:03:01,733 --> 00:03:08,000
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:03:08,133 --> 00:03:09,333
[GLASS CLINKS]

50
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,800
We built this together.

51
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:21,200
We'll work to make it bigger.

52
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:24,433
Mm-hmm.

53
00:03:24,567 --> 00:03:30,067
Lucas and Victor will carry
on what we started.

54
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:36,867
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES,
THEN FADES]

55
00:03:37,767 --> 00:03:39,467
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

56
00:03:41,633 --> 00:03:42,867
[DOOR OPENS]

57
00:03:44,033 --> 00:03:45,767
[WHISPERS] Mom.

58
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,167
Still awake?

59
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,033
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

60
00:03:52,333 --> 00:03:55,867
It's just hard to sleep
after everything.

61
00:04:00,167 --> 00:04:01,867
Yeah.

62
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,400
I am so proud of you.

63
00:04:05,533 --> 00:04:09,000
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:04:09,133 --> 00:04:10,933
Thank you, Mommy.

65
00:04:11,067 --> 00:04:13,267
You're always there for me.

66
00:04:14,467 --> 00:04:17,400
Thank you for being
so understanding.

67
00:04:20,533 --> 00:04:24,400
I know I messed up
with our family.

68
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:28,167
I try to make up for it
every single day.

69
00:04:29,933 --> 00:04:32,000
I keep trying to prove...

70
00:04:33,667 --> 00:04:35,867
...I'm a good daughter.

71
00:04:38,067 --> 00:04:41,167
I'm not perfect,

72
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:44,300
but I did my best.

73
00:04:44,433 --> 00:04:46,633
You don't have
to prove anything.

74
00:04:47,833 --> 00:04:49,100
Not to me...

75
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,167
or to anyone else.

76
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:56,967
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:04:57,100 --> 00:05:01,967
Uh... But I do to Dad.

78
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,867
I know...

79
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:11,433
I still need to earn
his love and forgiveness.

80
00:05:11,567 --> 00:05:16,433
If that day comes,
I'm willing to wait.

81
00:05:18,933 --> 00:05:20,967
I deserve this punishment.

82
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:24,233
No.
You know what you deserve?

83
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:29,367
You deserve
unconditional love.

84
00:05:30,933 --> 00:05:35,433
Your daddy may not be
giving you that right now,

85
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:39,733
but you deserve nothing less
than that.

86
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:44,633
That's kind of hard
to believe in.

87
00:05:44,967 --> 00:05:46,633
That I'm worthy of love.

88
00:05:46,767 --> 00:05:48,367
Don't say that.

89
00:05:49,533 --> 00:05:51,000
Don't think like that.

90
00:05:51,867 --> 00:05:55,533
What is the meaning
of being human?

91
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,333
It's to love.

92
00:05:59,167 --> 00:06:02,100
Don't deprive yourself of it.

93
00:06:04,833 --> 00:06:06,033
[SOBS]

94
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,567
I love you.

95
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:15,700
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:22,833
[SAM SOBBING]

97
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:34,333
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

98
00:06:34,733 --> 00:06:35,767
Django.

99
00:06:36,133 --> 00:06:37,400
Here's the money I earned.

100
00:06:40,533 --> 00:06:41,600
Is this all?

101
00:06:42,967 --> 00:06:44,833
I thought you had
a great catch?

102
00:06:44,967 --> 00:06:46,900
That's all inside his wallet.

103
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,767
What's the big idea?!

104
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:55,433
- Nothing?
- I told you, there's nothing!

105
00:06:57,433 --> 00:06:59,567
[NECKLACE JINGLING]

106
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,700
[CHAIR THUDS]

107
00:07:06,833 --> 00:07:07,933
What's this?

108
00:07:08,067 --> 00:07:09,267
That's mine.

109
00:07:09,833 --> 00:07:11,333
My girlfriend gave that to me.

110
00:07:12,267 --> 00:07:13,667
What a sweet girlfriend
you have there.

111
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,233
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS IN PAIN]

112
00:07:16,367 --> 00:07:18,300
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING IN PAIN]

113
00:07:18,433 --> 00:07:22,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:07:22,467 --> 00:07:23,733
[GUN COCKS]

115
00:07:26,033 --> 00:07:28,133
You know that I take down

116
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:30,200
everyone who messes with me.

117
00:07:30,333 --> 00:07:31,800
Please, Django...

118
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:36,800
But I won't do that to you.

119
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:39,867
Because you did get in
a lot of money after all.

120
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,833
So I'll spare you this time.

121
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:45,733
But don't ever show yourself
to me again.

122
00:07:46,033 --> 00:07:47,067
Do you understand?!

123
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,200
- Yes, Django.
- [BLOW LANDS]

124
00:07:48,367 --> 00:07:49,767
[THUDDING]

125
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:51,133
Get him out of my face.

126
00:07:51,267 --> 00:07:54,100
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GROANING IN PAIN]

127
00:07:54,233 --> 00:07:55,567
Get him out!

128
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:59,167
I'll get you some day, Django.

129
00:08:00,933 --> 00:08:05,667
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

130
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,533
[BINOY] I thought we were going
to strike it big.

131
00:08:07,667 --> 00:08:09,333
It's so hard to catch Mr. Chan.

132
00:08:09,467 --> 00:08:11,400
[TEKLA] Shut up! Stop whining.

133
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:14,367
It's not like Gabo wished
to let Tiger get away.

134
00:08:14,933 --> 00:08:17,200
[DABOY] Please, Gabo,
just give us something!

135
00:08:17,733 --> 00:08:19,267
[IPE] You're really not going
to stop, aren't you?

136
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:21,300
Want me to beat you up?

137
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:25,933
[TOLITS] I know that guy.

138
00:08:26,067 --> 00:08:27,833
He's one of Django's guys, Ben.

139
00:08:30,633 --> 00:08:31,667
Gabo.

140
00:08:32,367 --> 00:08:33,433
I'm Ben.

141
00:08:34,033 --> 00:08:35,567
I have something to tell you.

142
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,133
Why?

143
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,967
What do you need from Gabo?

144
00:08:42,433 --> 00:08:43,600
Gabo,

145
00:08:44,233 --> 00:08:46,700
my guilt has been eating me up
this past few days.

146
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,767
I know who shot your father,
Sir Rudy.

147
00:08:52,133 --> 00:08:53,267
[BLADE WHOOSHING]

148
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,767
- Gabo!
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING]

149
00:08:55,933 --> 00:08:57,400
Who shot my father?

150
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:58,867
Who was it?!

151
00:08:59,567 --> 00:09:01,067
It's Django, Gabo.

152
00:09:02,533 --> 00:09:03,700
Are you sure?

153
00:09:03,833 --> 00:09:04,767
Yes.

154
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:06,133
I saw it.

155
00:09:06,267 --> 00:09:07,667
We were together back then.

156
00:09:08,067 --> 00:09:10,333
During the riot
at the demolition.

157
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:12,600
If you're messing with me,

158
00:09:13,633 --> 00:09:15,867
I'll slit your throat open.
Understand?

159
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,167
- Huh?!
- Gabo!

160
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:19,467
[THUDDING]

161
00:09:20,033 --> 00:09:21,133
Gabo.

162
00:09:22,067 --> 00:09:23,600
Gabo, what now?

163
00:09:24,167 --> 00:09:26,733
Django will pay for what
he did to my father.

164
00:09:26,867 --> 00:09:28,900
[BREATHING SHARPLY]

165
00:09:29,067 --> 00:09:30,733
- Gabo!
- Come on!

166
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:36,500
[LAUGHING] That bastard Ben
thought he could get past me.

167
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:39,367
- [THUDDING]
- [GABO] Go ahead!

168
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:40,667
Just try and break free!

169
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,533
[INAUDIBLE]

170
00:09:42,667 --> 00:09:43,800
[BONG] Go ahead and try!

171
00:09:43,933 --> 00:09:45,300
Try me!

172
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:47,600
[BONG] Nobody move!

173
00:09:50,867 --> 00:09:52,200
You bastard.

174
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:54,367
So you're the one
who shot my father.

175
00:09:54,867 --> 00:09:56,300
- Huh?!
- [PAQUITO] Gabo!

176
00:09:56,433 --> 00:09:57,867
Ho-- hold on!

177
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,700
What are you talking about?

178
00:09:59,967 --> 00:10:01,333
It's this son of yours!

179
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:03,000
He shot my father!

180
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,133
And now he's at the hospital
fighting for his life!

181
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:09,067
Gabo, it wasn't me
who shot Sir Rudy!

182
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,133
Don't even try to fool me,
you bastard.

183
00:10:11,267 --> 00:10:12,533
Someone already spilled it!

184
00:10:12,667 --> 00:10:14,233
You know me, Gabo!

185
00:10:14,567 --> 00:10:16,833
If I'll get back at you,
I'll do it to you directly!

186
00:10:16,967 --> 00:10:19,300
I won't waste any time
on your father!

187
00:10:19,433 --> 00:10:21,433
A cop shot your father, Gabo!

188
00:10:21,567 --> 00:10:23,000
And everyone knows it!

189
00:10:23,133 --> 00:10:25,867
Gabo, let's talk this out!

190
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,500
Your accusation is not true!

191
00:10:28,633 --> 00:10:29,967
You know us!

192
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:32,200
If we were the ones
who shot Rudy,

193
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,533
he would've been
lying in a casket by now!

194
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:36,233
Who told you that anyway?!

195
00:10:36,833 --> 00:10:37,667
Ack!

196
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:38,900
Ben did!

197
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:41,833
Huh?

198
00:10:42,233 --> 00:10:43,600
I already fired him!

199
00:10:43,733 --> 00:10:45,500
Bastard stole from me!

200
00:10:45,633 --> 00:10:47,300
He just wanted
to get back at me!

201
00:10:49,567 --> 00:10:50,833
Gabo.

202
00:10:51,233 --> 00:10:52,833
Maybe what Django's saying
is true.

203
00:10:52,967 --> 00:10:54,000
[BONG] This is hard, Gabo.

204
00:10:54,133 --> 00:10:55,200
We're unsure about it.

205
00:10:55,333 --> 00:10:57,433
That Ben guy just came
out of the blue either.

206
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,500
Gabo, believe me.

207
00:10:59,633 --> 00:11:01,667
That bastard just wants
to see us fight!

208
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,567
[TEKLA] Gabo, let's go already!

209
00:11:04,267 --> 00:11:06,533
Django is a jerk
but he's got a point!

210
00:11:06,667 --> 00:11:08,967
If he wanted to get back at you,
he'll do it to you directly!

211
00:11:10,267 --> 00:11:12,633
- [GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]
- Ack!

212
00:11:12,767 --> 00:11:14,367
If I find out...

213
00:11:15,267 --> 00:11:17,100
that you were indeed the one
who shot my father...

214
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:19,267
I'll pick up where I left off.

215
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,733
[THUDDING]

216
00:11:20,867 --> 00:11:22,067
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

217
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,400
[BONG] Stay back!

218
00:11:23,867 --> 00:11:25,100
Stay back.

219
00:11:25,233 --> 00:11:29,100
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

220
00:11:29,233 --> 00:11:30,600
- Let's go.
- Quick!

221
00:11:31,033 --> 00:11:32,167
Let's move!

222
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:33,600
[GRUNTS]

223
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,300
You're really something.

224
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:44,433
You made Django and Gabo
fight each other.

225
00:11:44,433 --> 00:11:47,300
Well, doing that helped me
get back at Django.

226
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:49,900
I hope they both die.

227
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:51,300
[LAUGHTER]

228
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:52,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:55,300
- [THUD]
- [OBJECTS CLATTER]

230
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:59,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:11:59,133 --> 00:12:00,300
You lied to me!

232
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:03,600
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GROANING]

233
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,300
You bastard!

234
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:10,800
Who shot my father?!

235
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:11,800
It was Django.

236
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,400
He was the one
who shot your father.

237
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,333
Stop lying, you bastard!

238
00:12:16,367 --> 00:12:19,433
Django himself said that he
didn't shoot Mister Rudy.

239
00:12:19,433 --> 00:12:20,733
Damn you!

240
00:12:20,733 --> 00:12:24,267
You told Gabo that Django
shot Mister Rudy

241
00:12:24,267 --> 00:12:25,933
because Django's group
beat you up

242
00:12:25,933 --> 00:12:27,933
for stealing money
from them.

243
00:12:27,933 --> 00:12:31,133
That's how he plays, Gabo.
He has always been like that.

244
00:12:31,133 --> 00:12:33,333
He can't be trusted
with money.

245
00:12:33,333 --> 00:12:35,767
He lied to you so that
you and Django will fight

246
00:12:35,767 --> 00:12:37,133
while he gets his revenge.

247
00:12:37,133 --> 00:12:39,633
- You bastard!
- Ah!

248
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:41,100
How dare you put
Gabo in trouble!

249
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:43,467
- [GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

250
00:12:43,467 --> 00:12:45,767
- [GROANS]
- [KICK LANDS]

251
00:12:45,767 --> 00:12:46,967
[IPE] You deserve more
than that!

252
00:12:46,967 --> 00:12:51,767
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:54,733
And you?! What are you
all waiting for, huh?!

254
00:12:54,733 --> 00:13:00,700
- [CLAMORING]
- [OBJECTS CLATTER]

255
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:02,167
[THUD]

256
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:08,767
Gabo.

257
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:12,467
What's your plan now?

258
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,067
You guys go home.

259
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:18,800
Okay, Gabo.
We'll take it from here.

260
00:13:19,933 --> 00:13:21,600
- Let's go.
- Come on. Let's go home.

261
00:13:21,633 --> 00:13:23,633
- Clean up here, okay?
- Yeah.

262
00:13:23,633 --> 00:13:26,633
- We got this.
- Take care.

263
00:13:26,633 --> 00:13:28,733
Alright! Let's start cleaning!

264
00:13:28,733 --> 00:13:30,500
You know what to do.

265
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:32,400
They left us in charge here.

266
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:35,400
- There's money everywhere!
- Let's pick them up!

267
00:13:36,433 --> 00:13:39,900
- There's more over there!
- Look at all those coins!

268
00:13:42,167 --> 00:13:44,267
- [LIGHT FOOTSTEPS]
- [DOOR OPENS]

269
00:13:44,267 --> 00:13:46,000
- Good morning, ma'am.
- Good morning.

270
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,133
Your mom wants you to join
her for breakfast.

271
00:13:50,567 --> 00:13:53,833
- Have you called Max?
- I knocked at her room earlier.

272
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:55,567
But there was no answer.

273
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:57,200
She's probably still asleep.

274
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:02,000
Okay, you go ahead.

275
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,133
- I'll follow in a bit. Thanks.
- Okay, ma'am.

276
00:14:04,133 --> 00:14:07,433
[LIGHT FOOTSTEPS]

277
00:14:07,433 --> 00:14:09,200
[DOOR CLOSES]

278
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:12,433
[LIGHT FOOTSTEPS]

279
00:14:17,233 --> 00:14:20,767
[LIGHT FOOTSTEPS]

280
00:14:23,267 --> 00:14:25,667
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

281
00:14:25,667 --> 00:14:27,067
[SAM] Max?

282
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,200
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

283
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,367
Max?

284
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:37,267
Let's have breakfast together.

285
00:14:48,733 --> 00:14:53,067
I know that we have lots
of problems at work.

286
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,967
It can sometimes get toxic,

287
00:14:56,967 --> 00:15:00,233
and there are times we bring
our stress at home.

288
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:04,867
But I hope that we won't
let it affect us.

289
00:15:07,167 --> 00:15:10,733
We agreed that we'll have
each other's back, right?

290
00:15:10,733 --> 00:15:17,733
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

291
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:26,667
I'll go downstairs now, okay?

292
00:15:27,433 --> 00:15:28,967
I'll see you there.

293
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:36,967
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

294
00:15:47,167 --> 00:15:54,133
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

295
00:16:05,633 --> 00:16:12,633
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

296
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,800
[ISOBEL] Oh, hon!

297
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,667
Good morning!

298
00:16:18,667 --> 00:16:20,767
Breakfast is ready.

299
00:16:20,767 --> 00:16:23,500
I cooked it myself.

300
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:25,767
I'll just have some coffee.

301
00:16:25,767 --> 00:16:32,633
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

302
00:16:32,633 --> 00:16:34,600
Oh, Sam!

303
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:37,533
Come, dear.
Let's have breakfast.

304
00:16:37,533 --> 00:16:38,633
Come on.

305
00:16:39,967 --> 00:16:41,400
Here. Okay.

306
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:43,833
Just please. Sit down.

307
00:16:43,867 --> 00:16:45,100
Perfect!

308
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:48,800
Tell me if you want
anything else, okay?

309
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,633
I'll cook it for you.

310
00:16:50,633 --> 00:16:53,167
I don't want anything else.
Thank you.

311
00:16:53,167 --> 00:16:58,867
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

312
00:16:58,867 --> 00:16:59,933
[SIGHS LOUDLY]

313
00:17:01,833 --> 00:17:03,200
[ISOBEL] Oh!

314
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:05,133
Max, sit down.

315
00:17:05,133 --> 00:17:06,267
I'm not hungry, Ma.

316
00:17:06,267 --> 00:17:07,967
No, I insist!

317
00:17:07,967 --> 00:17:09,733
It's been so long since this
family's been complete

318
00:17:09,733 --> 00:17:11,067
on this table.

319
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:14,867
- Sorry, Ma. I'm just busy.
- No! Sit down!

320
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:21,833
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

321
00:17:35,933 --> 00:17:41,233
If you can't use your mouths
to eat the food in front of you,

322
00:17:41,233 --> 00:17:45,100
why don't you use them
to finally talk?

323
00:17:51,033 --> 00:17:52,333
[FRUSTRATED SIGH]

324
00:17:52,967 --> 00:17:56,833
Can't anyone appreciate
what I'm doing here?!

325
00:18:00,467 --> 00:18:01,600
- Thank you for breakfast.
- Thank you for breakfast.

326
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:04,100
No, I'm not talking
about the food!

327
00:18:05,733 --> 00:18:07,733
I'm talking about us!

328
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:11,467
Can't we go back
to being a family

329
00:18:11,467 --> 00:18:14,233
who gathers around
the dining table

330
00:18:14,233 --> 00:18:16,733
to talk and enjoy the food?!

331
00:18:16,733 --> 00:18:19,867
Don't blame yourself if we
can't be complete anymore...

332
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:23,967
...in the same way
that I don't blame you

333
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,433
for hoping that
could still happen again.

334
00:18:27,433 --> 00:18:29,867
[ISOBEL] Ricardo, I'm not
blaming myself

335
00:18:30,667 --> 00:18:33,300
because I know
I'm doing enough

336
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:34,867
for my family.

337
00:18:36,133 --> 00:18:38,267
We may not be complete.

338
00:18:38,267 --> 00:18:40,600
But we are still a family.

339
00:18:42,067 --> 00:18:45,000
But sometimes, I wonder...

340
00:18:46,233 --> 00:18:48,500
Can we still consider this
a family

341
00:18:50,033 --> 00:18:53,233
with the way
we treat each other?

342
00:18:55,767 --> 00:18:59,033
I keep trying to
fix things among you.

343
00:18:59,033 --> 00:19:02,067
I keep trying
to prevent you from fighting.

344
00:19:02,067 --> 00:19:06,867
Because all I want
is for us to be a normal family.

345
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:12,167
And I am not asking you
to appreciate me!

346
00:19:12,167 --> 00:19:16,700
I just want you to show
some care for each other!

347
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:23,567
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

348
00:19:32,067 --> 00:19:33,400
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

349
00:19:35,467 --> 00:19:37,233
My god...

350
00:19:37,233 --> 00:19:39,167
I give up!

351
00:19:39,167 --> 00:19:41,300
Suit yourselves!

352
00:19:42,367 --> 00:19:49,367
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

353
00:20:03,067 --> 00:20:10,033
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:20:12,167 --> 00:20:14,733
Well, Gabo? Did you manage
to secure some money?

355
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:18,967
Will you just wait
until your father flatlines

356
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:20,833
before you do something?!

357
00:20:20,833 --> 00:20:23,433
Do I have to do
everything again?!

358
00:20:23,433 --> 00:20:26,000
I almost sold my body
to find us some cash!

359
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,633
Are you really just going to
sit there and do nothing?

360
00:20:28,633 --> 00:20:30,733
You're going to leave this
on me again?!

361
00:20:32,267 --> 00:20:33,533
Don't worry.

362
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:37,667
I'll find a way so Papa
can have his operation.

363
00:20:38,533 --> 00:20:40,167
I promise I'll find a job.

364
00:20:40,167 --> 00:20:43,500
All you do is make
promises you can't keep!

365
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:44,767
That's enough!

366
00:20:45,567 --> 00:20:49,033
Betchay, could you please
go easy on Gabo?

367
00:20:49,033 --> 00:20:51,033
The kid's doing his best!

368
00:20:51,033 --> 00:20:52,567
He already promised--

369
00:20:52,567 --> 00:20:58,833
I don't need promises!
What I need is money!

370
00:20:58,833 --> 00:21:01,200
I'm begging you, Gabo!

371
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:04,267
We need money! Money!

372
00:21:04,267 --> 00:21:08,633
And you think yelling at him
is going to help us?!

373
00:21:08,667 --> 00:21:10,633
- Oh god.
- We should use this time...

374
00:21:10,633 --> 00:21:13,033
...to think of how we
can afford Rudy's operation

375
00:21:13,033 --> 00:21:14,467
and save him!

376
00:21:15,467 --> 00:21:16,967
My goodness, Gabo!

377
00:21:16,967 --> 00:21:18,433
[DISAPPOINTED SIGH]

378
00:21:18,433 --> 00:21:20,667
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

379
00:21:24,333 --> 00:21:25,800
[VIA] Good morning, Sam!

380
00:21:26,333 --> 00:21:27,500
- Good morning.
- Oh!

381
00:21:27,833 --> 00:21:30,333
Will you request
for a CCTV footage too?

382
00:21:31,067 --> 00:21:32,000
Of what?

383
00:21:32,133 --> 00:21:33,233
Of Chinatown.

384
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:36,300
Ma'am Pia asked for a copy.

385
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:40,200
- Is that so?
- She talked to us

386
00:21:40,333 --> 00:21:41,300
one by one last night.

387
00:21:41,433 --> 00:21:44,100
She asked us about the mission.

388
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,633
- What did you tell her?
- The truth.

389
00:21:47,767 --> 00:21:49,967
That if only Sir Seb hadn't
messed things up,

390
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:51,533
our mission would have
gone smoothly.

391
00:21:51,667 --> 00:21:54,467
But no! He still fought
with that man.

392
00:21:54,933 --> 00:21:56,100
Wait.

393
00:21:57,167 --> 00:21:58,200
Who is that guy?

394
00:21:58,733 --> 00:21:59,900
Was he the one who kissed you?

395
00:22:01,667 --> 00:22:03,767
The truth is...
I don't know him.

396
00:22:04,333 --> 00:22:05,600
One thing's for sure,

397
00:22:06,067 --> 00:22:09,300
I'd love to meet him
so I can finally catch him.

398
00:22:10,467 --> 00:22:11,767
He's pissing me off so bad.

399
00:22:13,433 --> 00:22:14,400
[CLEARS THROAT]

400
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:18,167
Team leader!

401
00:22:18,433 --> 00:22:19,500
Why are you here?

402
00:22:19,633 --> 00:22:22,567
I've been staying up all night
reviewing your mission.

403
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:26,667
Good luck.

404
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:33,267
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:35,067
- [KNOCKING ON DOOR]
- Sir?

406
00:22:35,733 --> 00:22:36,767
Yes?

407
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:42,600
This is the report on
what happened in Chinatown.

408
00:22:51,133 --> 00:22:52,433
Are you sure about this report?

409
00:22:52,567 --> 00:22:54,567
Yes. It's impartial.

410
00:22:54,700 --> 00:22:57,967
That's based off of happened
and what the agents have said.

411
00:22:58,267 --> 00:22:59,667
"Agent Tuazon's performance

412
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:02,633
throughout the operation
that led to the arrest

413
00:23:02,767 --> 00:23:05,467
of Victor Zafra was exemplary

414
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:07,300
and reflected the highest

415
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:11,800
standard expected of NCIA

416
00:23:12,533 --> 00:23:13,533
personnel."

417
00:23:14,133 --> 00:23:15,400
Is he that good?

418
00:23:15,833 --> 00:23:17,833
Hmm... well...

419
00:23:18,567 --> 00:23:20,667
Based on my investigation,

420
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:25,400
Sebastian was the one
who carried out the mission.

421
00:23:25,767 --> 00:23:28,433
Sam just took the credit.

422
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:29,867
Took credit?

423
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,267
Sir, please read the report.

424
00:23:32,633 --> 00:23:34,867
The truth won't deceive you.

425
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:42,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

426
00:23:46,100 --> 00:23:47,433
We've been going
around in circles.

427
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:49,500
I think we should ask around.

428
00:23:50,667 --> 00:23:53,600
No. It's just straight ahead.

429
00:23:56,767 --> 00:23:58,033
Estrella, stay here.

430
00:23:58,800 --> 00:24:01,000
They might change their minds
when they see you.

431
00:24:01,133 --> 00:24:02,367
Stay here and wait for me.

432
00:24:04,033 --> 00:24:06,633
Hello!
Can I ask a few questions?

433
00:24:06,767 --> 00:24:09,567
Do you know where
Rudy Magtibay lives?

434
00:24:09,700 --> 00:24:11,100
The one who got shot
during the demolition?

435
00:24:11,233 --> 00:24:13,033
Why? What do you need from them?

436
00:24:13,167 --> 00:24:15,433
We'll only provide assistance.

437
00:24:16,500 --> 00:24:17,767
[MAN] They live there.

438
00:24:18,333 --> 00:24:19,267
- Here?
- [MAN] Yes, that's it.

439
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:21,233
Oh, right here! Thank you.

440
00:24:24,733 --> 00:24:26,467
Hello, is anyone there?

441
00:24:26,867 --> 00:24:29,633
- Hello!
- Who are you?

442
00:24:30,367 --> 00:24:34,133
[MAX] Is this where
Rudy Magtibay lives?

443
00:24:34,267 --> 00:24:36,367
The one who got shot
during the demolition?

444
00:24:36,500 --> 00:24:39,367
- Yes, I'm his sister.
- [BETCHAY] I'm his wife.

445
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:40,600
Oh, hello!

446
00:24:40,733 --> 00:24:41,667
- [BETCHAY] Hello.
- [GABO] Who are you?

447
00:24:41,800 --> 00:24:44,800
Ah, this is Gabo,
Rudy's son.

448
00:24:44,933 --> 00:24:49,167
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

449
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:50,367
[MAX] Ah...

450
00:24:51,467 --> 00:24:53,700
I'm here to give financial aid.

451
00:24:54,033 --> 00:24:54,933
To Rudy.

452
00:24:55,633 --> 00:24:56,600
You're here to help?

453
00:24:57,767 --> 00:24:59,133
Why? What organization
do you work for?

454
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:01,367
From...

455
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:02,800
from NGO!

456
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:06,233
We usually provide help
to those in need.

457
00:25:06,367 --> 00:25:09,133
- I know that! Come inside!
- [MAX] Oh, alright!

458
00:25:09,267 --> 00:25:10,600
- Come in.
- Wait a minute.

459
00:25:10,733 --> 00:25:15,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

460
00:25:15,833 --> 00:25:18,400
You don't look like you work
for NGO.

461
00:25:21,633 --> 00:25:23,800
If you came here
to settle this,

462
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:25,433
you're making a mistake.

463
00:25:27,233 --> 00:25:28,733
Because we won't.

464
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:32,900
I'll make the one
who shot my father pay.

465
00:25:36,533 --> 00:25:37,700
I work for NGO.

466
00:25:37,833 --> 00:25:40,400
I'm here to give
Rudy's financial aid

467
00:25:40,533 --> 00:25:41,800
to help his hospitalization.

468
00:25:41,933 --> 00:25:43,700
This could really help him.

469
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:51,267
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

470
00:25:55,567 --> 00:25:56,633
This is a lot.

471
00:25:57,567 --> 00:25:58,667
I'm sorry.

472
00:25:59,267 --> 00:26:01,333
[ENVELOPE THUDS]

473
00:26:01,467 --> 00:26:03,067
Hey, stop.

474
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:04,367
We could really use that money!

475
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:06,033
Stop meddling!

476
00:26:06,167 --> 00:26:07,667
- Why not?
- Miss.

477
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,500
If you came here to buy us off,

478
00:26:10,833 --> 00:26:12,033
you're mistaken.

479
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:15,500
You can't pay off
my fathers hospitalization!

480
00:26:16,033 --> 00:26:17,867
And I'll make sure, that whoever
did that to my father,

481
00:26:18,833 --> 00:26:20,267
will rot in jail!

482
00:26:20,667 --> 00:26:24,900
We won't talk to you,
especially if you're a cop!

483
00:26:25,267 --> 00:26:26,367
You're stepping out of line!

484
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:28,533
My brother's life is in danger,

485
00:26:28,667 --> 00:26:31,000
and you have the nerve
to do this to us!

486
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:34,800
You should leave.

487
00:26:35,667 --> 00:26:36,900
You might get involved in this.

488
00:26:38,100 --> 00:26:40,500
Before I lose
my temper with you.

489
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:43,900
Leave!

490
00:26:44,033 --> 00:26:51,033
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

491
00:27:00,300 --> 00:27:04,600
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

492
00:27:04,733 --> 00:27:07,467
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

493
00:27:07,600 --> 00:27:08,767
[MAMENG] Gabo.

494
00:27:08,900 --> 00:27:10,000
Gabo!

495
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:12,367
Please, just understand
that woman.

496
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:15,633
Maybe she just really
wants to help us.

497
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:16,867
Why, Auntie?

498
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,333
Just what do they think?

499
00:27:18,467 --> 00:27:19,800
That just because we're poor

500
00:27:19,933 --> 00:27:21,600
we can sell our dignity
so easily?

501
00:27:21,733 --> 00:27:22,933
No!

502
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:25,867
Whoever shot Father
will definitely be imprisoned!

503
00:27:26,733 --> 00:27:29,400
Even if it takes your father's
life in exchange?

504
00:27:29,533 --> 00:27:36,500
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

505
00:27:42,900 --> 00:27:44,167
[CLATTERS]

506
00:27:44,567 --> 00:27:45,700
[RATTLES]

507
00:27:55,567 --> 00:27:56,733
[DOOR OPENS]

508
00:27:58,233 --> 00:28:05,233
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

509
00:28:05,867 --> 00:28:07,100
[DOOR CLOSES]

510
00:28:08,533 --> 00:28:10,167
So, Attorney, can I go now?

511
00:28:10,300 --> 00:28:13,233
Victor, we're doing everything
we can to get you out--

512
00:28:13,367 --> 00:28:14,967
If you're doing
everything you can,

513
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:17,167
I would've been
out of here already!

514
00:28:17,433 --> 00:28:18,767
But where am I right now?

515
00:28:18,900 --> 00:28:21,067
[VICTOR] Where? Am I free?

516
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:22,467
Tell me!

517
00:28:22,633 --> 00:28:25,200
We have to go through
a lot of process--

518
00:28:25,333 --> 00:28:27,233
That's because you're weak!

519
00:28:27,733 --> 00:28:29,100
You're weak.

520
00:28:29,700 --> 00:28:33,233
My family should've gotten me
a better lawyer.

521
00:28:33,367 --> 00:28:34,733
[INHALES SHARPLY]

522
00:28:34,867 --> 00:28:36,433
Get me out of here
as soon as possible.

523
00:28:36,567 --> 00:28:38,833
Yes, uh, of course!

524
00:28:38,967 --> 00:28:42,100
And look for the man
who the group fought with.

525
00:28:42,233 --> 00:28:45,567
Because it's his fault
that I'm here right now.

526
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:49,533
I'll make sure he pays
for everything he did myself.

527
00:28:49,667 --> 00:28:56,633
[GRIM MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

528
00:29:00,067 --> 00:29:01,300
<i>They said that I violated
a lot of rules.</i>

529
00:29:01,433 --> 00:29:03,000
And that I'm not a good leader.

530
00:29:03,133 --> 00:29:04,167
<i> I could even get suspended.</i>

531
00:29:04,300 --> 00:29:05,933
<i>Congratulations!
You did a great job.</i>

532
00:29:06,067 --> 00:29:07,067
<i> There's no celebration.</i>

533
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:08,800
<i>Especially if there's a threat
of suspension.</i>

534
00:29:08,933 --> 00:29:09,967
<i> Threat of suspension?!</i>

535
00:29:10,100 --> 00:29:12,167
<i>Ihman is coming today
to take the motorcycle!</i>

536
00:29:12,300 --> 00:29:14,100
<i>- He's taking it back!
- I'll call the police on you!</i>

537
00:29:14,233 --> 00:29:15,400
<i> You utterly failed!</i>

538
00:29:15,533 --> 00:29:16,767
<i> It was about to be sold!</i>

539
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:18,867
So your father could finally get
<i> an operation!</i>

540
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:21,000
<i> We almost had it!</i>

541
00:29:21,133 --> 00:29:23,233
<i>Find the woman
who kidnapped Victor.</i>

542
00:29:23,367 --> 00:29:24,800
<i> Tell me who that man is.</i>

543
00:29:24,933 --> 00:29:26,400
<i>Investigate it yourself.
You're good right?</i>

544
00:29:26,533 --> 00:29:28,733
<i>He'll pay for what he did
to Victor.</i>

545
00:29:28,900 --> 00:29:30,667
I really need to find that man.

546
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:32,267
<i>How are we gonna start
tracking that guy down?</i>

547
00:29:32,400 --> 00:29:34,167
<i>The motorcycle.
It will lead the way</i>

548
00:29:34,300 --> 00:29:35,800
<i> for me to find him.</i>

549
00:29:35,933 --> 00:29:37,567
<i>We need to get
the motorcycle back immediately.</i>

550
00:29:37,700 --> 00:29:38,700
[THUDS]

551
00:29:38,833 --> 00:29:40,933
<i>We'll get caught here
if we're not cautious!</i>

552
00:29:41,433 --> 00:29:43,567
<i>We need to find
Gabo's motorcycle!</i>

553
00:29:43,900 --> 00:29:45,567
<i>I believe
that guy is the key</i>

554
00:29:45,700 --> 00:29:47,700
<i>for us to solve
this gold smuggling case.</i>

555
00:29:47,833 --> 00:29:51,133
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [MAN GRUNTING]

556
00:29:51,267 --> 00:29:52,400
<i> Let's search the whole place.</i>

557
00:29:52,533 --> 00:29:53,967
<i>I need to get
the motorcycle back.</i>

558
00:29:54,100 --> 00:29:55,500
[ENGINE REVVING]
